/F2 18 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 790 Tm (Toy Room Inventory - Test Document) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 743 Tm (1. Bag A) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 721 Tm (Bag A contains 8 blue balls and 10 red balls.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 701 Tm (Bag A is made of green canvas and is kept on the top shelf.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 681 Tm (Each blue ball in Bag A weighs 50 grams. Each red ball weighs 40 grams.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 641 Tm (2. Bag B) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 619 Tm (Bag B contains 5 green balls, 3 blue balls and 2 yellow balls.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 599 Tm (Bag B is a small leather bag kept under the desk.) Tj
/F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 559 Tm (3. Box C) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 537 Tm (Box C holds 12 wooden cubes and 4 toy cars. It does not contain any balls.) Tj
/F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 517 Tm (Box C is owned by Priya. Bag A and Bag B are owned by Arjun.) Tj
